+## Failure during session initialization
+
+- When `beforeSession` throws an `Error`, the orchestrator awaits `onError(session, error)` with the original session and error, then awaits `afterSession(session)` before rejecting with the original error (provided those hooks complete normally). No user-input or model processing follows the failed initialization. `afterSession` is cleanup for an attempted turn, not proof that initialization completed: it must tolerate no allocation or partial allocation, and hooks must track their own acquired resources; no new session-started flag is supplied ([validated by: reports and cleans up a beforeSession failure before rejecting with the original error](../../src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.acceptance.test.ts#L7)).
+
